<title>CANADA: Canada Nov wage settlements rise average 1.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Nov wage settlements rise average 1.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Annual wage increases in Canadian collective bargaining agreements reached in November averaged 1.9 percent, down from 2.7 percent in October, the Department of Human Resources Development said on Tuesday</p>
<p>			   Agreements/employees    Pct change</p>
<p>Public sector	  8/16,424		     +0.5</p>
<p>Private sector	 6/19,610		     +3.0</p>
<p>Wage increases are the average annual percentage increase in base rates -- the wage rate of the lowest paid classification in a bargaining unit -- over the term of the agreement in settlements negotiated during the period shown.</p>
<p>(For more information on the settlements, contact Human Resources Development's Workplace Information Directorate, at 1-800-567-6866 or 819-997-3117.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
